<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ari Malla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1200–1216</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Arideva Malla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ari Malla was the first king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a> to bear the Malla title, beginning the Malla period of Nepalese history around 1200. The dynasty he began ruled the valley until the Gorkha conquest of 1768 to 1769, shaping Newar culture, art and architecture.</p></div>
